        {
            "number": 4,
            "revision": "a41b62f57299a98f97dea8c3b345b8ba2033db92",
            "parents": [
                "8c90746e306e999d21965886166099fb054252e4"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/43/89543/4",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                "username": "jaehyoo"
            },
            "createdOn": 1779339246,
            "author": {
                "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                "username": "jaehyoo"
            },
            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE_WITH_MESSAGE_UPDATE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jeremy Kerr",
                        "email": "jk@ozlabs.org",
                        "username": "jk-ozlabs"
                    },
                    "message": "Looks good, a couple of minor things inline.\n\n\nOverall though: have you tested with other compression types? busybox tar requires different options for gzip (`-x`) vs bz2 ('-j`) vs xz (`-J`), but your detection logic only adds `-x` for any of those three.\n\nOn the other hand, GNU tar does the autodetection itself, so doesn't need any `-x` option, we should check whether just using that is simpler...."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "You're right. Patchset #4 only supported gzip, so in patchset #5 I added support for all supported compression formats except lzma, and tested them all.\n\nAs you mentioned, the current BusyBox tar v1.37 in the OpenBMC build was compiled with CONFIG_FEATURE_TAR_AUTODETECT enabled, so compression formats are automatically detected and handled. However, the current extraction logic in this code uses a pipe, which prevents the autodetection from working.\n\nI added a more detailed explanation about the reason in the commit message, so please take a look."
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc/software_utils.cpp",
                    "line": 32,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jeremy Kerr",
                        "email": "jk@ozlabs.org",
                        "username": "jk-ozlabs"
                    },
                    "message": "minor nit: this doesn't really tell us that this is a compressed _tar_ file, just that it is compressed. Maybe `isCompressed()` ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc/software_utils.cpp",
                    "line": 32,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "+1"
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc/software_utils.cpp",
                    "line": 32,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "In patch set #5, I improved the handling logic for each compression format. Could you please take a look?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc/software_utils.cpp",
                    "line": 36,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jeremy Kerr",
                        "email": "jk@ozlabs.org",
                        "username": "jk-ozlabs"
                    },
                    "message": "You can use `pread()` to avoid the `lseek()`."
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc/software_utils.cpp",
                    "line": 36,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "+1"
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc/software_utils.cpp",
                    "line": 36,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "Yeah, that looks much cleaner. In patch set #5, I changed it to use pread()."
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc/software_utils.cpp",
                    "line": 41,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jeremy Kerr",
                        "email": "jk@ozlabs.org",
                        "username": "jk-ozlabs"
                    },
                    "message": "The bzip2 and xz checks have their own check of bytesRead, why not just include this check in the gzip case too?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc/software_utils.cpp",
                    "line": 41,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "+1, only gzip references first 2 bytes for now (other conditions already have size check), so better to keep it as first check for gzip."
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc/software_utils.cpp",
                    "line": 41,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "I also improved this part by restructuring it to use a per-format handling table."
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc/software_utils.cpp",
                    "line": 62,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jeremy Kerr",
                        "email": "jk@ozlabs.org",
                        "username": "jk-ozlabs"
                    },
                    "message": "You could also make these three checks a little less hard-coded with an array of magic bytes that you check for; that would save the multiple-array-index checks, and make it easier to support new formats in future.\n\n\nThe downside is the complexity of the array-of-arrays-of-chars, but there can be neat ways to define that.\n\n(however, this may become preferable if we add support for `-j` / `-J` too)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc/software_utils.cpp",
                    "line": 62,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the good suggestion. I incorporated this feedback into patch set #5 as well."
                }
            ],
