            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for reviewing this and for pointing out the areas that needed fixes and improvements. I addressed all of the feedback and updated the implementation accordingly, so could you please take another look?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "I also created another fix that approaches the problem differently:\n\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-bmc-code-mgmt/+/90489\n\nInstead of using a pipe for the problematic tarball image, it handles the image through a seekable file descriptor and delegates the compression type autodetection to tar itself, which I think results in a cleaner implementation."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jeremy Kerr",
                        "email": "jk@ozlabs.org",
                        "username": "jk-ozlabs"
                    },
                    "message": "(btw I do like the new table approach, looks good)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc/software_utils.cpp",
                    "line": 45,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jeremy Kerr",
                        "email": "jk@ozlabs.org",
                        "username": "jk-ozlabs"
                    },
                    "message": "Super minor, but you don't need to repeat the bytes in the comment.\n\nAlso, -xf are repeated in call cases - I think your previous approach of just specifying the one compression argument was good. This is a bit weird in that you're providing part of a pair of arguments with the `-f` included."
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc/software_utils.cpp",
                    "line": 45,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "Good point. The code itself already explains that part, so there\u2019s no need to repeat it in the comments. Also, since -xf is common across all options, it doesn\u2019t make sense to duplicate it in the table either. I\u2019ve cleaned all of that up in patch set #7, so please take another look."
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc/software_utils.cpp",
                    "line": 54,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jeremy Kerr",
                        "email": "jk@ozlabs.org",
                        "username": "jk-ozlabs"
                    },
                    "message": "Can you tie this size to the definition of TarFormat.magic?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc/software_utils.cpp",
                    "line": 54,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "Sure. Having a separate array length member in the table was also redundant, and it felt like the kind of thing that could easily become a maintenance weak point later if someone adds an incorrect length number. I changed it to use the actual array size directly instead of a magic-number length field, and refactored it using std::vector."
                }
            ],
