            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for your valuable comments. I\u2019ve addressed all of the feedback and updated everything in patch set #7, so could you please take another look?\n\nAlso, I submitted what I think may be a cleaner alternative fix here:\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-bmc-code-mgmt/+/90489\n\nCould you compare the two approaches and share your thoughts on which one looks better?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jeremy Kerr",
                        "email": "jk@ozlabs.org",
                        "username": "jk-ozlabs"
                    },
                    "message": "I like the approach of the alternative, but I think the implementation needs some changes; have commented there."
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc/software_utils.cpp",
                    "line": 75,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jeremy Kerr",
                        "email": "jk@ozlabs.org",
                        "username": "jk-ozlabs"
                    },
                    "message": "super minor, but I'd suggest splitting the arguments so you're not pasting too much together:\n\n```\n    tarCmd = \"tar -x \" + (possibly -z / -j / -J / etc) + \" -f \" + filename\n\n```\n\n... but only if you're re-rolling for other reasons."
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc/software_utils.cpp",
                    "line": 75,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "Yeah, this looks better. In the case of LZMA, this change still doesn\u2019t fully cover it because of the irregular header pattern issue. However, considering that we may need to support compression types in the future that require explicit options like --lzma, I think your suggested approach is more flexible overall.\n\nI updated the implementation in patch set #8, so please take another look."
                }
            ],
